  "prompt": "You are a senior analyst in the Westlake Capital Markets equity research team. James Marchetti needs a margin variance model for Home Depot ahead of next week's client discussions. The FY2026 10-K (period ending February 2026) has just been filed; we need to analyze the QoQ margin movement versus the prior quarter.\n\nBuild an Excel workbook with the analysis. Use the attached historical summary for context on prior periods.\n\n- The model must contain a clear QoQ margin variance analysis for HD's gross margin, operating margin, and net margin.\n- Use the pinned annual revenue of $164,683M and gross profit of $54,865M for the latest period (Q1 FY2026). Source the comparative prior-quarter (Q4 FY2025) figures from the most recent 10-Q filing if the 10-K does not provide quarterly segments.\n- Calculate each margin as a percentage of revenue and show both the absolute and basis-point change QoQ.\n- Decompose the gross margin variance into its key drivers where the data is available (e.g., COGS components).\n- Break out SG&A as a percentage of revenue and flag any line items moving more than 50 bps.\n- Include a summary table at the top that calls out the two or three largest margin movers with a one-line driver note for each.\n- Format all dollar figures in millions with one decimal place, and percentages to two decimal places. Negative variances must be in red or parentheses.\n- Use standard sell-side tab structure: Summary, Revenue, Margins, SG&A Detail, Source Notes. Ensure the Source tab notes the specific EDGAR filing (citing the XBRL concept names and filing dates) for every data point. The workbook should be clean and presentation-ready with consistent formatting and no merged cells.",
