    "explicit_requirements": [
      "Build an Excel workbook with a QoQ margin variance analysis for Home Depot covering gross margin, operating margin, and net margin using the most recent annual filing period and prior comparable period data from SEC EDGAR.",
      "Calculate each margin line item as a percentage of revenue and show the absolute and basis-point change quarter-over-quarter.",
      "Decompose gross margin variance into the key drivers where data is available from the filing (COGS components, occupancy, shrinkage, etc.).",
      "Break out SG&A as a percentage of revenue and show the QoQ change, noting any line items that moved more than 50 bps.",
      "Include a summary table at the top of the workbook that flags the two or three largest margin movers with a brief one-line annotation per driver.",
      "Use the pinned revenue figure of $164.683B and gross profit of $54.865B for the latest period; source prior-quarter estimates from the most recent 10-Q if the 10-K does not segment quarterly data.",
      "Ensure all dollar figures are in millions with one decimal, and percentages are carried to two decimal places throughout."
    ],
    "implicit_requirements": [
      "Workbook tabs should follow a standard sell-side convention: Summary, Revenue, Margins, SG&A Detail, Source Notes.",
      "Every data cell must trace back to a specific EDGAR filing line item; include a Source tab or footnotes with XBRL concept names and filing dates.",
      "Negative variance items (margin compression) should be formatted in red or parenthetical notation per banking convention.",
      "Column headers must include period labels with fiscal quarter identifiers (e.g., Q1 FY2026 vs Q4 FY2025), not just dates.",
      "The workbook should be presentation-ready: consistent font, number formatting, no gridlines on the Summary tab, print area set to fit on one landscape page."
    ],
